From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:03:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 333/333] DOS-PORT: patch 0333 -- MIDI status reports SDL
 0255's OPL window pacing and peak arrivals

WHY: SDL 0255 paces OPL writes on a PicoGUS so that no 2.57 ms window of
the card's drain carries more than 128, because the card overwrites its
command buffer silently and nothing on the host can see it. Whether the
pacing engaged, what it cost the ISR, and the most writes that actually
landed in one window must be in every run's record: the peak is the only
host-side witness of the card's buffer occupancy.

WHAT: the isr-mode fragment of audio_vital_status gains
pace=<K>/<window_us>, pwait=<waits>/<total_us>/<longest_us> and
peak=<arrivals upper bound>/<ring overruns>, from SDL_DOSOplPaceStats. The
wait time is inside isr_ns_per_write's numerator (0250's drain time), so a
per-write cost without the waits is (isr_sum - total_us) / writes. The
fragment's worst case grows from 606 to 699 characters (every %u at 10
digits, %llu at 20, each %s at its buffer), so the fragment buffer grows
640 -> 768 and the two status buffers 1024 -> 1280.

SDL references renumbered 2026-09-25 with the SDL series (0223 -> 0250,
0224 -> 0251, 0228 -> 0254, 0229 -> 0255). This is the pump-free cut: it
lands on main before the RTC pump series (ags 0277-0282), which re-applies on
top and then owns the combined buffer sizing (the max of every need).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
